Illegal Reporting Without Original Creditor Authorization or Valid Contract Under the FCRA and Fair Debt Collection Practices Act ( FDCPA ), it is unlawful for a debt collector or third-party entity to report a tradeline if : The account did not originate with the reporting entity, The consumer does not have a contractual relationship with the reporting entity, and There is no documentation proving a legal assignment or ownership of the debt. 

As confirmed in XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, debt collectors and furnishers who claim ownership of or report debts without evidence of assignment or authority are in violation of 15 U.S.C. 1692e, which prohibits false, deceptive, and misleading representations.

