The failure to correct inaccurate credit reporting upon notice of dispute constitutes willful violation of the FCRA. Cortez v. Trans Union , LLC, 617 F.3d 688 ( 3d Cir. 2010 ) This notice serves as a final opportunity to resolve this matter privately and in good faith. Silence is acquiescence, and failure to respond with complete and verified documentation will be construed as fraudulent concealment and tacit admission of all claims herein.

