13347554,2025-05-05,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Information belongs to someone else,"this formal complaint regarding XXXX XXXX, which is reporting a collection account on my credit file. I dispute their legal authority to collect on this alleged debt, as they are not the original creditor and have failed to provide me with any verifiable documentation proving they have a legal assignment or ownership of this debt. 
XXXX XXXX is reporting a collection account on my credit report. However, they are not listed as the original creditor, and they have not supplied me with any signed contract or legally binding assignment agreement that shows they are authorized to collect this debt or report it to the credit bureaus. 
Fair Debt Collection Practices Act ( FDCPA ) 15 U.S.C. 1692g : I have the right to request validation of the debt. XXXX must provide evidence of the amount owed, the name of the original creditor, and documentation that proves they own or have been assigned the debt. To date, they have not provided sufficient validation. 


Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ) 15 U.S.C. 1681i and 1681s-2 : Any information on my credit report must be accurate and verifiable. If a creditor can not verify an account, it must be deleted. XXXX  failure to prove its claim means this debt should not appear on my credit report. 


Uniform Commercial Code ( UCC ) Article 9, 9-406 : According to UCC 9-406 ( c ), if a debtor ( myself ) requests proof of assignment, the collector ( XXXX  ) must furnish it. Without valid documentationsuch as the original contract bearing my ink signature or a legally executed assignmentthey have no standing to collect or report this debt. 


UCC 3-305 & 3-309 Enforcement of Instruments : Under these codes, a party attempting to enforce a negotiable instrument ( like a debt ) must prove they are the holder or a non-holder in possession with the rights of a holder. If the original contract has been lost or destroyed, they must meet strict conditions. XXXX has provided no such evidence. 


