13440379,2025-05-09,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Improper use of your report,Reporting company used your report improperly,"XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, GA XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX XXXX, NV XXXX Subject : Demand to Cease Reporting Transactions to Consumer Reporting Agencies per 15 U.S.C. 1681a ( d ) ( 2 ) ( A ) ( i ) Account # XXXX Dear XXXX, I am writing to respectfully demand that you immediately cease reporting certain transactions or experiences, including any late payments, associated with my account XXXX to any consumer reporting agency ( e.g., Equifax, XXXX, XXXX  ), as these transactions are excluded from the definition of a consumer report under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), specifically 15 U.S.C. 1681a ( d ) ( 2 ) ( A ) ( i ). 

The following items are transactions or experiences solely between me and XXXX, and their reporting to consumer reporting agencies is improper : 1. Late payment reported for [ XX/XX/year> ] on account XXXX This is a transaction or experience solely between me and XXXX, as it reflects my direct payment activity with you. 
