3. Late payment reported for [ XX/XX/year> ] on account XXXX This is a transaction or experience solely between me and XXXX, as it reflects my direct payment activity with you. 
4. Late payment reported for [ XX/XX/year> ] on account XXXX This is a transaction or experience solely between me and XXXX, as it reflects my direct payment activity with you. 
5. Late payment reported for [ XX/XX/year> ] on account XXXX This is a transaction or experience solely between me and XXXX, as it reflects my direct payment activity with you. 

Under 15 U.S.C. 1681a ( d ) ( 2 ) ( A ) ( i ), the term consumer report does not include any report containing information solely as to transactions or experiences between the consumer and the person making the report. My payment history, including any late payments, constitutes a record of transactions or experiences solely between me and you, the creditor. Therefore, these transactions are explicitly excluded from the FCRAs definition of a consumer report and should not be reported to consumer reporting agencies. 

Furthermore, the reporting of payment history is a standard of the Fair Isaac Corporation ( FICO ) scoring model, not a requirement or definition under 15 U.S.C. 1681a or any other provision of the FCRA. As such, you lack legal authority under the FCRA to report these transactions to consumer reporting agencies, and doing so violates the intent of the exclusion in the FCRA.",,"EQUIFAX, INC.",GA,315XX,,Web,2025-05-09,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes
