Under the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), consumer reporting agencies are required to maintain reasonable procedures to ensure the maximum possible accuracy of consumer information [ 15 U.S.C. 1681e ( b ) ]. Additionally, when a consumer files a dispute, credit bureaus must conduct a reasonable reinvestigation and delete or correct inaccurate or unverifiable information within 30 days [ 15 U.S.C. 1681i ( a ) ].

