13753543,2025-05-28,Debt collection,Credit card debt,Communication tactics,"Used obscene, profane, or other abusive language","I am filing this complaint regarding two phone calls I had with representatives from Midland Credit Management ( MCM ) regarding a debt they have acquired. 

The first call was on XX/XX/year>, and lasted approximately 17 minutes. During this call, the representative was extremely pushy, rude, and at times difficult to understand. He attempted to pressure me into immediately signing an agreement electronically while I was driving. I explained that I was unable to safely access a device while on the road and would need to wait until I reached my destination. He insisted that the agreement had to be signed right now or it would be void and Id have to start the process over. When I expressed surprise, he became more aggressive and said something to the effect of why did you even call if you werent ready to do this now? I ended the call feeling rushed, disrespected, and uneasy. 

The second call took place on XX/XX/year>, and lasted about 7 minutes before I was placed on hold indefinitely. This representative was more polite, but continued the same high-pressure tactics. She repeatedly told me that enrolling in a payment plan using a bank account or debit card would freeze the account and prevent further legal actionbut simply sending payments by money order or cashiers check would not protect me. I explained that I had been advised not to provide my banking information, but she continued to claim that entering it into a phone or website wasnt giving it to the company. That is misleading and falseif I enter my checking account number to make payments, then the company clearly has the ability to withdraw money. 

I also explained that I was not refusing to payI just did not want to give sensitive financial data. She acknowledged that they would accept mailed payments but continued to push the idea that only a formal plan with bank info would stop legal action. When I pushed back, she eventually asked me to hold, and never returned to the line. 

These calls left me feeling misled, pressured, and manipulated. I believe Midland Credit Management is engaging in deceptive practices by : Insisting that only electronic payments will stop legal action Refusing to work with me unless I give my banking information Rushing me into a legally binding agreement without a chance to review it properly Using emotional manipulation and pressure tactics to force compliance I am willing to pay what I owe, but I should not be coerced into handing over sensitive financial data to do so. I hope the CFPB will review these tactics as I believe they are unethical and potentially unlawful.",,ENCORE CAPITAL GROUP INC.,WI,53143,,Web,2025-05-28,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes
